course: dictionary
lesson: 1497
title: Names of peoples and places
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Cayuga is a name. It can name a people, a language or a lake. Names like this start with a capital letter, even in the middle of a sentence.
explain: Context tells you which Cayuga is meant. «The Haudenosaunee Confederacy united the Mohawk, Oneida, Onondaga, Cayuga and Seneca, later the Tuscarora, under a Great Law of Peace; clan mothers chose chiefs and could remove them.» Here Cayuga sits in a list of peoples, so it names a people.
explain: Look for clue words. Words like lake, shore or water tell you it is Cayuga Lake. Words like speak or language tell you it is the Cayuga language. Ask yourself: what kind of thing is being talked about?
fact: Cayuga is a proper name, so it always starts with a capital letter.
fact: «Cayuga» can mean the Cayuga people, a Native American (First Nations) people from what is now New York State and Ontario.
fact: «Cayuga» can also mean the Cayuga language, spoken by that people.
fact: «Cayuga» names Cayuga Lake, one of the Finger Lakes in New York State, and places named after it.
fact: The Cayuga are one of the Six Nations of the Haudenosaunee (Iroquois) Confederacy.
exercise: «The Cayuga are one of the Six Nations of the Haudenosaunee Confederacy.» What does Cayuga name here? | A river | A type of bird | A mountain | *A people
exercise: Which one means Cayuga Lake, one of the Finger Lakes? | The Mohawk people | The Haudenosaunee Confederacy | *Cayuga Lake | The Cayuga language
exercise: Why does Cayuga start with a capital letter? | It always starts a sentence | It is a colour | It is a very long word | *It is a proper name
test: In «the Cayuga language», what does Cayuga name? | A forest | A kind of bread | A town square | *A language
test: In which place is Cayuga Lake found? | *New York State | Wales | Australia | Scotland
exam: Which clue shows that Cayuga is a name and not an ordinary word? | The word has six letters | *The capital C | It is in the middle of a sentence | The full stop at the end
